  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 146 PM EDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nThe long term picks up as a weak system is expected to work it's way \nthrough the SE. The GFS has come into line with the Euro, showing \nthe likelihood of receiving more than a half of inch of rain has \nfallen to less than 50% across the CWA. While showers and possibly a \nrumble of thunder are possible Saturday night into Sunday morning, \nwe aren't expecting anything significant in terms of potential \nprecipitation. As a result, Sunday doesn't look like the washout we \nhave been expecting.\n\nAny lingering precip will clear out late Sunday afternoon and we'll \nhave another few days of pleasant weather with highs in the low to \nmid 70s before a stronger low pressure system pushes in from the \nGreat Plains on Wednesday. There is still some uncertainty in the \nforecast when it comes to rainfall totals and coverage, but temps \nare expected to fall into the upper 60s and low 70s after the front \npasses with overnight lows falling back towards the upper 40s by the \nsecond half of the work week.",
